post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
Spade65 is in the application menu as "Spade65".

A udev rule granting hidraw access was installed, and pacman's udev hook has
already reloaded it. A keyboard that was plugged in before this install keeps
its old permissions until it is replugged, or until:

  sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw

The rule tags the device with uaccess, so the signed-in user gets access
without joining a group.

On a KDE session that was already running, the entry appears in the launcher
but without its icon: plasmashell reads newly installed desktop entries and
keeps its own icon cache. Restart the shell once, or sign out and back in:

  systemctl --user restart plasma-plasmashell.service
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
